        <briefdescription>
<para>Reads the system clock. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>On Windows, the current time is captured via <computeroutput>timespec_get()</computeroutput> with <computeroutput>TIME_UTC</computeroutput>. On POSIX platforms with <computeroutput>CLOCK_MONOTONIC</computeroutput> defined, <computeroutput>clock_gettime(CLOCK_MONOTONIC)</computeroutput> is used to obtain a monotonic reading. On platforms where neither macro is defined, <computeroutput>ts</computeroutput> is left unchanged.</para>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="out">ts</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The <computeroutput>timespec</computeroutput> where the reading is stored. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="par"><title>Returns</title><para>Nothing. </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
